## Competency Framework

# Select the competencies relevant to your course. Delete those not used.

### Written Production Competencies (WP)
- WP1 — Write a structured scientific abstract (structured / unstructured)
- WP2 — Write an IMRAD research article section (Intro / Methods / Results / Discussion)
- WP3 — Produce a lab report (undergraduate level)
- WP4 — Write a literature review paragraph with citation integration
- WP5 — Write a poster abstract and caption text
- WP6 — Produce a cover letter or research grant summary

### Oral/Multimodal Competencies (OM)
- OM1 — Deliver a 10-minute scientific presentation (slides)
- OM2 — Present a scientific poster in English
- OM3 — Participate in a Q&A session after a talk
- OM4 — Conduct a simulated peer review discussion

### Critical Reading Competencies (CR)
- CR1 — Identify the IMRAD structure of a research article
- CR2 — Evaluate the quality of a scientific abstract
- CR3 — Perform a structured peer review of a classmate's text
- CR4 — Critically analyse the methodology section of a paper

### Language Competencies (LC)
- LC1 — Use hedging language appropriately
- LC2 — Manage tense usage across IMRAD sections
- LC3 — Build complex noun phrases for precision
- LC4 — Use academic vocabulary (AWL + domain-specific)
- LC5 — Maintain register consistency throughout a text

